    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a mixed slate today, but the setup is particularly favorable for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Kyle Tucker** (74.44), who represent our strongest plays. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a massive 14% dynamic platoon boost against the right-handed Holmes, combined with an ideal #2 spot in the order. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** is in a prime position to produce; despite facing a lefty, his base projection is so elevated that he remains a must-start, while **Andy Pages** (69.18) rounds out our top-tier outfield production against Gasser, whose 5.63 xERA provides the most exploitable matchup of the day. We are banking on these top-three anchors to provide the bulk of our R and RBI production.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup optimizer was the omission of **Nolan Schanuel** (44.77). While he presents a stable floor, he was sidelined in favor of **Dominic Smith** (57.31) and **Jackson Merrill** (56.09), both of whom offered higher efficiency scores derived from superior platoon environments or park advantages. We continue to navigate a challenging landscape with **Gunnar Henderson** forced to the bench due to a confirmed rainout, and we remain without the services of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** as they continue their recovery on the IL.\n\nInvestors should monitor the matchup for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.94) closely; while he is in the lineup, he faces the toughest assignment of the day in Skenes (2.96 xERA). The significant 19% penalty for opposing pitcher skill drags down his high base projection, leaving him as a borderline start that we are relying on for pure talent rather than matchup favorability. Outside of the weather risk for our post-poned assets, the priority remains maximizing SB efficiency where possible, though the day\u2019s favorable xERA matchups for **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci** suggest a high-floor outcome for our infield core.",
